  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific standing Metekhi church: mapped stone body with intersecting gables, three projecting eastern apses and metal cap roofs, twelve-sided drum with narrow real window apertures/blind arched surrounds, grey conical standing-seam roof and metal cross. Projecting north porch has a gabled brick/stone front, real pointed side arches, two narrow front windows and a recessed timber church entrance. Shared ashlar/brick/metal textures, original simplified archivolts/lozenge relief and short local approaches. Natural cliff, terrace, river, monument and independent buildings remain host context. No full ritual interior or copied inscription/stone inventory.",
    "identityBasis": "Exact-QID Q20577625/way1064270003 and named standard PMTiles building/POI35185436358835 identify the whole church. Six subordinate mapped building parts identify main body35184412940804, north porch35185436358834, three apses35185579262555..557 and drum35185579262558. Anchor44.811256736,41.690155211; heading0, internal local+x angle-1.484066758501rad (approximately north), local+z approximately east toward the apses. Roof/gable splits, door/window positions and hidden details are ordinary-picture/map-led allocations inside these envelopes.",
    "heightBasis": "Retained catalog scale about24.5m above local church floor,20m long/16m core width, checked against ordinary pictures and mapped body/porch/apse/drum envelopes. Main wall about11m, cross-gable ridges14m, drum14.4..19.8m, conical metal cap19.8..23.3m and cross24.5m. Central apse about10.3m wall, flanks8.3m with low cap roofs; north porch5m eaves/7.4m gable. Catalog heights and map-part heights are approximate visualization cues, not surveyed construction dimensions; window/arch stations, patching, hidden facades and exact masonry courses are approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain original standard6m Mapzen urban/cliff terrain, water and every independent building. A small local level church plinth has constant grade-buried bottom edges sampled along the actual parent envelope; short porch approaches connect toward native grade. No broad cliff/terrace slab, flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse DEM does not resolve cliff face, exact paved terrace, stairs or threshold levels; these remain approximate host context.",
